WebKit: auxiliary processes without the application's descriptors

The process launcher let the web and network processes inherit every
descriptor of the application (so that GLib could use posix_spawn()). On
the reference a web view's processes get nothing of the application's.
An application that streams a page through a pipe of its own (TextMate's
HTML output, through an NSURLProtocol) never saw the pipe's end: the web
process, started after the pipe was made, held its write end open. On
Darwin the launcher now passes only the descriptors it hands over, and
GLib closes the rest in the child.

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/Launcher/glib/ProcessLauncherGLib.cpp
@@ -231,7 +231,16 @@
     // must not use a child setup fuction.
     //
     // Please keep this comment in sync with the duplicate comment in XDGDBusProxy::launch.
+#if OS(DARWIN)
+    // Minkar: the auxiliary processes get only the descriptors given to them
+    // (g_subprocess_launcher_take_fd()), as the reference's do. Inheriting
+    // the application's kept the write end of a pipe it had made open in the
+    // web process, and the application never saw the pipe's end (TextMate's
+    // HTML output, 24 Nov 2026). GLib closes the others after fork().
+    GRefPtr<GSubprocessLauncher> launcher = adoptGRef(g_subprocess_launcher_new(G_SUBPROCESS_FLAGS_NONE));
+#else
     GRefPtr<GSubprocessLauncher> launcher = adoptGRef(g_subprocess_launcher_new(G_SUBPROCESS_FLAGS_INHERIT_FDS));
+#endif
     int webkitClientSocketValue = webkitSocketPair.client.release();
     g_subprocess_launcher_take_fd(launcher.get(), webkitClientSocketValue, webkitClientSocketValue);
 
